│ patch_description        │ The batch-based pipeline in `pipelined_ssd_to_gpu` was serializing SSD reads and GPU      │
│                          │ copies: it submitted a batch of reads, waited for ALL to complete, then did all GPU       │
│                          │ copies. This prevented overlap between I/O and DMA transfers.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Fix: Converted to a sliding-window pipeline (matching the zero-copy variant's design).    │
│                          │ Now each completed NVMe read immediately triggers a GPU H2D copy, and the next NVMe read  │
│                          │ is submitted right away. This overlaps SSD I/O with GPU DMA transfers. Also increased     │
│                          │ PIPELINE_RING_SIZE to 16 for deeper NVMe queue depth.                                     │
