│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ sliding_window_pipeline_overlap                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The batch-based pipeline loop serialized SSD reads and GPU copies - it submitted all      │
│                          │ reads in a batch, waited for all completions, then did all GPU copies. This prevented any │
│                          │ overlap between I/O and compute. Fixed by implementing a sliding-window approach: prime   │
│                          │ the ring with initial reads, then for each completion immediately issue the GPU copy and  │
│                          │ submit the next read. This overlaps SSD I/O with GPU DMA transfers. Also increased        │
│                          │ PIPELINE_RING_SIZE from 8 to 16 to better saturate the NVMe queue depth.                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
