│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ sliding_window_pipeline_overlap                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The original pipeline loop used a batch approach: submit N reads, wait for ALL N to       │
│                          │ complete, then copy all to GPU. This serializes I/O and GPU DMA, resulting in low         │
│                          │ throughput and high latency.                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The fix converts the pipeline loop to a true sliding-window approach: as each individual  │
│                          │ NVMe read completes, immediately start the GPU DMA copy for that chunk and submit the     │
│                          │ next NVMe read. This overlaps SSD I/O with GPU transfers, significantly improving         │
│                          │ throughput and reducing latency. Also increased PIPELINE_RING_SIZE to 16 for deeper queue │
│                          │ depth.                                                                                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
